gates.prompt:
Parse these git commits and generate a structured CHANGELOG entry:

Commits:
{{git_commits}}

Version: {{current_version}}
Repo: {{repo_url}}

Produce a JSON response with:
1. features: array of { title, description, commit_hash }
2. fixes: array of { title, description, commit_hash }
3. refactors: array of { title, description, commit_hash }
4. summary: one-line release summary

Format commit messages as readable titles (remove hash prefix). Group by category.

Update README.md with the new release. Context:

Version: {{current_version}}
Changelog data: {{changelog-analyzer}}
Repo: {{repo_url}}

Your tasks:
1. Update version badge to {{current_version}}
2. Add or update "What's New" section with top 3 features/fixes
3. Add changelog link: [CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md#v{{current_version}})
4. Keep existing README structure, only modify version-related sections

Return JSON:
{
  "sections_updated": ["what's-new", "badge", "changelog-link"],
  "changes_summary": "Human-readable summary of what was changed",
  "file_content": "Complete updated README.md content"
}

Update roadmap status based on release. Context:

Version released: {{current_version}}
Features in this release: {{changelog-analyzer.features}}
Repo: {{repo_url}}

Your tasks:
1. Review existing roadmap.md or README roadmap section
2. Mark features in {{changelog-analyzer.features}} as ✓ DONE
3. Propose 3-5 next steps based on open GitHub issues (if available)
4. Estimate effort for each next step (Low/Medium/High)

Return JSON:
{
  "completed_items": ["feature-1", "feature-2"],
  "next_items": [{"title": "", "effort": "Low|Medium|High", "description": ""}],
  "roadmap_content": "Updated roadmap.md or roadmap section (if exists)",
  "has_roadmap_file": true|false
}
